From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:23:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] daemon: RCS chat through IMSroha when it is there

A transport next to SMS/MMS: IMSroha's codes.noa.IMSroha.Rcs on the
system bus (imsroha-rcs, opt-in there). While the service is absent or not
registered nothing changes. When it is registered, a 1-to-1 text to a number
whose OPTIONS say chat goes as RCS; SendMessage refusing it, or a failed
status before it was sent, sends the same message as SMS. Received RCS
messages are stored with transport rcs; delivered and displayed IMDNs land
in deliveryReport and readReport; reading the chat sends the displayed
notifications. isComposing goes both ways: setComposing on the daemon's
D-Bus interface, and a composingChanged signal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L5scTQJJDo2PTt6GBeDFah
